WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:28.480
Well, howdy doody boys and girls, and howdy doody, Roddy, all right?

00:28.480 --> 00:31.960
Hi there, howdy doody. Hi, kids at home. Hi, Clarabelle.

00:31.960 --> 00:34.480
And look at all the wonderful kids in the peanut gallery.

00:34.480 --> 00:35.880
Hi, kids. What time is it?

00:35.880 --> 00:38.280
Happy New Year!

00:38.280 --> 00:40.280
You're right. Let's sing the theme.

00:40.280 --> 00:42.280
Okay, professor, here we go.

00:42.280 --> 00:47.480
It's Happy New Year!

00:47.480 --> 00:50.480
It's Happy New Year!

00:50.480 --> 00:53.480
Come on, let's sing the song.

00:53.480 --> 00:56.480
Come on, let's sing the song.

00:56.480 --> 01:02.480
Let's give a round of cheers for Happy New Year!

01:02.480 --> 01:05.480
It's time to start the show.

01:05.480 --> 01:08.480
So kids, let's go!

01:08.480 --> 01:10.480
Wait, everybody, kids. Hi, everybody.

01:10.480 --> 01:12.480
Hi, Howdy. How you doing?

01:12.480 --> 01:14.480
Oh, hi, Ray.

01:14.480 --> 01:17.480
Gee, I'm glad to see your ukulele is okay today.

01:17.480 --> 01:18.480
Oh, you bet.

01:18.480 --> 01:22.480
Not much good without the strings and the way that Clarabelle fixed it yesterday.

01:22.480 --> 01:26.480
That's right, Howdy. They're all on there now. I've got all my strings on me.

01:26.480 --> 01:30.480
Say, you know something else, Ray? Crossing the street isn't very good either.

01:30.480 --> 01:31.480
That's right.

01:31.480 --> 01:33.480
I mean, if you don't use your eyes as well as your feet.

01:33.480 --> 01:36.480
What would you like to hear my song about it?

01:36.480 --> 01:38.480
I certainly wouldn't, Howdy.

01:38.480 --> 01:39.480
Okay.

01:39.480 --> 01:43.480
Well, if you think you'll use your feet when you cross the street,

01:43.480 --> 01:48.480
I'll set you wise in the daytime or night.

01:48.480 --> 01:53.480
Look around left and right and cross the street with your eyes.

01:53.480 --> 01:59.480
If you look before you leap, you will always keep the hell few prize.

01:59.480 --> 02:06.480
It is safer to wait, be a few seconds late, and cross the street with your eyes.

02:06.480 --> 02:13.480
Never try to beat that car, even though it's off so far.

02:13.480 --> 02:22.480
Chances are you won't be seen, so don't take a step till the light turns green.

02:22.480 --> 02:29.480
If you think you'll use your feet when you cross the street, here's a surprise.

02:29.480 --> 02:36.480
Your pal Howdy knows if you have 50 toes, you still cross the street with your eyes.

02:36.480 --> 02:38.480
Say, what's about one more song?

02:38.480 --> 02:40.480
Oh, thanks, kids.

02:40.480 --> 02:43.480
And say, Ray, would you come here a minute, please?

02:43.480 --> 02:44.480
Sure, Howdy.

02:44.480 --> 02:45.480
What is it?

02:45.480 --> 02:46.480
Bend over a minute, please.

02:46.480 --> 02:49.480
I want to whisper something to you, Ray.

02:49.480 --> 02:52.480
Will you sing out the...

02:52.480 --> 02:54.480
Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.

02:54.480 --> 02:57.480
And I sing away to you every and every...

02:57.480 --> 02:58.480
That's fine.

02:58.480 --> 02:59.480
And I sing...

02:59.480 --> 03:01.480
All right, all right, Howdy.

03:01.480 --> 03:03.480
I think that's a wonderful idea.

03:03.480 --> 03:06.480
Kid, Howdy just told me of a wonderful game that we can play,

03:06.480 --> 03:09.480
and it's going to require two children from the peanut gallery.

03:09.480 --> 03:10.480
A boy and a girl.

03:10.480 --> 03:12.480
Maybe this little boy over here.

03:12.480 --> 03:13.480
Come on out here.

03:13.480 --> 03:15.480
And this little girl, all right?

03:15.480 --> 03:16.480
She's my friend.

03:16.480 --> 03:18.480
Oh, well, I'm very glad that she's your friend.

03:18.480 --> 03:20.480
Come on out here, kids.

03:20.480 --> 03:25.480
Now, we're going to show you how very, very important it is to use your eyes.

03:25.480 --> 03:27.480
Now, first I want to know your name, dear.

03:27.480 --> 03:28.480
Ricky.

03:28.480 --> 03:30.480
Oh, say it real loud.

03:30.480 --> 03:31.480
Ricky.

03:31.480 --> 03:33.480
And where do you come from, Ricky?

03:33.480 --> 03:35.480
Where are you from?

03:35.480 --> 03:39.480
From Watson Avenue.

03:39.480 --> 03:40.480
From Watson Avenue?

03:40.480 --> 03:42.480
Where is it?

03:42.480 --> 03:43.480
Baton Rouge.

03:43.480 --> 03:44.480
Well, good.

03:44.480 --> 03:45.480
And how about your name?

03:45.480 --> 03:46.480
I'm Billy.

03:46.480 --> 03:47.480
Billy what?

03:47.480 --> 03:48.480
Billy Tate.

03:48.480 --> 03:49.480
Billy Tate.

03:49.480 --> 03:50.480
And where are you from, Billy?

03:50.480 --> 03:51.480
Mobile.

03:51.480 --> 03:53.480
Mobile where?

03:53.480 --> 03:54.480
Mobile, Alabama.

03:54.480 --> 03:55.480
Alabama.

03:55.480 --> 03:56.480
And you're all the way up here in New York?

03:56.480 --> 03:57.480
Well, that's wonderful.

03:57.480 --> 04:00.480
Now, look, I'll tell you what we're going to do, kids.

04:00.480 --> 04:02.480
This is a very interesting game.

04:02.480 --> 04:07.480
Clarabelle has a blindfold here, and we're going to blindfold the little boy,

04:07.480 --> 04:12.480
and then he's going to be turned around, and you're going to have to pick for a prize

04:12.480 --> 04:14.480
that's going to be hanging on a string, see?

04:14.480 --> 04:16.480
But you won't be able to see what you get.

04:16.480 --> 04:19.480
And then the little girl is going to be able to pick for a prize later,

04:19.480 --> 04:21.480
but she will be able to see.

04:21.480 --> 04:24.480
Now, we'll explain to you what goes on after you get the prize, all right?

04:24.480 --> 04:26.480
Go ahead, Clarabelle.

04:26.480 --> 04:31.480
Now, how about letting down the prizes, Clarabelle?

04:31.480 --> 04:33.480
Oh, there, I see them coming now.

04:33.480 --> 04:34.480
Oh, wait a minute, wait a minute now.

04:34.480 --> 04:36.480
Wait a minute, you stand right here, okay?

04:36.480 --> 04:37.480
You watch what's going on.

04:37.480 --> 04:41.480
This is a very, very important game.

04:41.480 --> 04:44.480
Okay, now, are you all ready, Clarabelle?

04:44.480 --> 04:49.480
All right, now, let's turn Billy around so he won't know just exactly in what direction he's going.

04:49.480 --> 04:52.480
Now, go right directly ahead and hold your hands out,

04:52.480 --> 04:55.480
and the first prize that you get will be yours.

04:55.480 --> 04:58.480
Go ahead.

04:58.480 --> 05:00.480
That's it, Clarabelle.

05:00.480 --> 05:01.480
Where's my sister?

05:01.480 --> 05:04.480
Oh, here they are.

05:04.480 --> 05:05.480
There we are.

05:05.480 --> 05:06.480
Now, you hold that.

05:06.480 --> 05:07.480
No, leave it on, leave it on.

05:07.480 --> 05:08.480
Can't see.

05:08.480 --> 05:11.480
Now, we'll let the little girl try for a prize.

05:11.480 --> 05:13.480
Don't go away, Billy, you stay right here.

05:13.480 --> 05:18.480
Now, I just happen to have a piano stool that you can get up on

05:18.480 --> 05:21.480
if you want a different kind of a prize, see?

05:21.480 --> 05:23.480
Would you like to get up on there?

05:23.480 --> 05:25.480
Do you see anything you'd like?

05:25.480 --> 05:26.480
Yeah?

05:26.480 --> 05:27.480
All right, come on.

05:27.480 --> 05:28.480
Come on.

05:28.480 --> 05:30.480
Oh, my goodness, what a big girl.

05:30.480 --> 05:32.480
Now, which prize do you think you'd like?

05:32.480 --> 05:33.480
That one?

05:33.480 --> 05:34.480
All right.

05:34.480 --> 05:38.480
You do it.

05:38.480 --> 05:39.480
There you are.

05:39.480 --> 05:40.480
Looking.

05:40.480 --> 05:42.480
Now, come on over here, Billy.

05:42.480 --> 05:44.480
Here, now let me see.

05:44.480 --> 05:45.480
You can take your blindfold off.

05:45.480 --> 05:46.480
Now, that's a boy.

05:46.480 --> 05:48.480
Give that back to Clarabelle.

05:48.480 --> 05:49.480
Wait a minute, wait a minute.

05:49.480 --> 05:50.480
Now, look.

05:50.480 --> 05:53.480
Here is the whole point of the game.

05:53.480 --> 05:57.480
Now, Billy, because he had a blindfold on and he couldn't see,

05:57.480 --> 06:00.480
went over there and he picked a prize,

06:00.480 --> 06:02.480
and all it is is a bunch of old newspapers.

06:02.480 --> 06:05.480
But you, because you could see, you got up on the piano stool

06:05.480 --> 06:07.480
and you got a wonderful prize, didn't you?

06:07.480 --> 06:08.480
Isn't that right?

06:08.480 --> 06:13.480
Well, now, Clarabelle, just because this was a demonstration kind of a game,

06:13.480 --> 06:15.480
have you got a prize for Billy?

06:15.480 --> 06:16.480
Real prize?

06:16.480 --> 06:18.480
All right.

06:18.480 --> 06:23.480
Oh, another Howdy Doody puppet, just like the one that Ricky has.

06:23.480 --> 06:24.480
Do you know how to work it, Billy?

06:24.480 --> 06:25.480
Yeah.

06:25.480 --> 06:26.480
You put your hand up inside of it here.

06:26.480 --> 06:29.480
See, you put your hand right inside.

06:29.480 --> 06:30.480
Yeah.

06:30.480 --> 06:32.480
And you put your finger up in there, and then you make it work,

06:32.480 --> 06:33.480
and then you talk.

06:33.480 --> 06:34.480
Here.

06:34.480 --> 06:36.480
Okay?

06:36.480 --> 06:37.480
How do you make it talk?

06:37.480 --> 06:39.480
Oh, you have to talk for it.

06:39.480 --> 06:41.480
Okay, kids, thank you very much.

06:41.480 --> 06:43.480
I think that was a wonderful game, don't you?

06:43.480 --> 06:44.480
Yeah.

06:44.480 --> 06:49.480
See, that demonstrates how very important it is to be able to see

06:49.480 --> 06:51.480
and always remember to look where you're going.

06:51.480 --> 06:52.480
Isn't that right, Howdy?

06:52.480 --> 06:53.480
Wasn't that great?

06:53.480 --> 06:54.480
Oh.

06:54.480 --> 06:55.480
Gee, I hope so, Ray.

06:55.480 --> 06:58.480
And kids, really, you don't know how important it is.

06:58.480 --> 07:01.480
Sometimes a man driving your car can't see you,

07:01.480 --> 07:04.480
and anyway, it's you who has to use your eyes.

07:04.480 --> 07:05.480
That's right.

07:05.480 --> 07:07.480
No one else can ever do that for you.

07:07.480 --> 07:08.480
That's right.

07:08.480 --> 07:09.480
It's very...

07:09.480 --> 07:12.480
Very well said, Howdy.

07:12.480 --> 07:14.480
Very well said.

07:14.480 --> 07:15.480
Howdy, Mr. Buster.

07:15.480 --> 07:17.480
Well, thank you very much.

07:17.480 --> 07:19.480
Yes, you were 100% correct.

07:19.480 --> 07:22.480
Now, whether you're young or old,

07:22.480 --> 07:25.480
or North American or South American,

07:25.480 --> 07:28.480
you must keep your eyes open all the time.

07:28.480 --> 07:29.480
Oh, that's right, Mr. Buster.

07:29.480 --> 07:32.480
I know you always keep your eyes open.

07:32.480 --> 07:34.480
Oh, yes, indeedy, I do.

07:34.480 --> 07:38.480
And right now, my eyes are open, and do you know what they see?

07:38.480 --> 07:40.480
No, what do they see?

07:40.480 --> 07:43.480
They see the Blusteroo chart.

07:43.480 --> 07:44.480
Oh.

07:44.480 --> 07:46.480
Yes, Howdy, the Blusteroo chart.

07:46.480 --> 07:48.480
But do you know what they don't see?

07:48.480 --> 07:49.480
No.

07:49.480 --> 07:52.480
What is it they don't see is if I didn't know.

07:52.480 --> 07:55.480
Hmm, well, you have a good imagination.

07:55.480 --> 07:59.480
They don't see anything on the chart for yesterday.

07:59.480 --> 08:02.480
You didn't give 500 marbles to me yesterday,

08:02.480 --> 08:07.480
and you didn't give me something else instead of the marbles either.

08:07.480 --> 08:09.480
Oh, I know, Mr. Buster, but you weren't here yesterday,

08:09.480 --> 08:13.480
and how could I give you anything if you weren't even here even?

08:13.480 --> 08:16.480
That's a good point, but it's just an excuse.

08:16.480 --> 08:18.480
But the answer is simple enough, Howdy.

08:18.480 --> 08:20.480
You owe me something for yesterday,

08:20.480 --> 08:22.480
and of course, you owe me something for today.

08:22.480 --> 08:26.480
So today, you will give me two things.

08:26.480 --> 08:28.480
Oh, dear, that's right, I guess.

08:28.480 --> 08:29.480
Yes.

08:29.480 --> 08:32.480
Well, I don't have any marbles for you, Mr. Buster,

08:32.480 --> 08:34.480
so what would you like first?

08:34.480 --> 08:37.480
Well, now, I was thinking this morning,

08:37.480 --> 08:41.480
hmm, some time ago, you gave me the scope doodle.

08:41.480 --> 08:44.480
Yeah, that's right. You own the scope doodle now.

08:44.480 --> 08:46.480
And I was thinking,

08:46.480 --> 08:50.480
what good is the scope doodle without the scope doodle curtains?

08:50.480 --> 08:53.480
Oh, you mean those nice red curtains that Clarabelle opens up

08:53.480 --> 08:55.480
when he goes to the scope doodle?

08:55.480 --> 09:00.480
Specifically, yes, those nice red curtains.

09:00.480 --> 09:01.480
I might take those.

09:01.480 --> 09:03.480
Oh, well, I guess that's all right.

09:03.480 --> 09:06.480
Curtains won't do me much good if I don't own the scope doodle.

09:06.480 --> 09:12.480
Yes, but before I take the things, I'd like a demonstration.

09:12.480 --> 09:16.480
Oh, Clarabelle, would you be kind enough to open and close

09:16.480 --> 09:19.480
the scope doodle curtains four times for me?

09:19.480 --> 09:23.480
Yes, four times. That should be a fair test.

09:23.480 --> 09:28.480
Yes, Clarabelle, please do it for Mr. Buster, will you?

09:28.480 --> 09:31.480
That's fine, Clarabelle, you're doing very well.

09:31.480 --> 09:35.480
All right, now do it three more times, please.

09:35.480 --> 09:38.480
Mm-hmm, that's right.

09:38.480 --> 09:41.480
All right, Clarabelle's very clever, isn't he, Mr. Buster?

09:41.480 --> 09:43.480
Oh, exceptionally, yes, he is.

09:43.480 --> 09:45.480
I didn't think he knew how to pull a string.

09:45.480 --> 09:49.480
He's done this so well that I'll take the curtains

09:49.480 --> 09:51.480
and I'll count them as 500 marbles.

09:51.480 --> 09:53.480
Oh, thank you, Mr. Buster.

09:53.480 --> 09:56.480
Clarabelle, will you please fix the Buster route chart?

09:56.480 --> 09:57.480
Write down curtains on the left.

09:57.480 --> 09:59.480
That's right.

09:59.480 --> 10:02.480
That's it, and then 2,000 in the other column.

10:02.480 --> 10:05.480
That's a pretty big number for him.

10:05.480 --> 10:08.480
That's it, now you take care of that, Clarabelle.

10:08.480 --> 10:11.480
Mr. Buster, that settles it on yesterday's marbles,

10:11.480 --> 10:15.480
but now I have to give you 500 more for today.

10:15.480 --> 10:16.480
That's right.

10:16.480 --> 10:18.480
What do you want to offer me?

10:18.480 --> 10:21.480
I got lots more curtains, Mr. Buster.

10:21.480 --> 10:23.480
Oh, no, no, no, thank you.

10:23.480 --> 10:24.480
I don't want any more curtains.

10:24.480 --> 10:26.480
Enough is enough.

10:26.480 --> 10:28.480
What else do you have left to give me?

10:28.480 --> 10:30.480
Well, I just don't know right now.

10:30.480 --> 10:31.480
I have so little left.

10:31.480 --> 10:33.480
Well, would you give me some time to think about it,

10:33.480 --> 10:36.480
and later I'll try to have something ready for you.

10:36.480 --> 10:39.480
All right, certainly, I'll be back in a few minutes,

10:39.480 --> 10:43.480
but I want something, and it better be good.

10:43.480 --> 10:47.480
Goodbye, and greetings, greetings, greetings, gentlemen.

10:47.480 --> 10:48.480
Goodbye.

10:48.480 --> 10:50.480
Goodbye, Mr. Buster.

10:50.480 --> 10:52.480
I'll have something for you.

10:52.480 --> 10:55.480
Ray, would you come here a second, please?

10:55.480 --> 10:56.480
Yes, Harvey, do it.

10:56.480 --> 10:58.480
Is there anything I can do for you?

10:58.480 --> 11:02.480
Oh, yes, I just gave Mr. Buster the scope doodle curtains

11:02.480 --> 11:04.480
to take care of yesterday's marbles, but...

11:04.480 --> 11:05.480
Yes.

11:05.480 --> 11:07.480
Well, gee whiz, I have to give him something for today, too,

11:07.480 --> 11:09.480
and I'm stumped.

11:09.480 --> 11:11.480
I wonder if you could think of something.

11:11.480 --> 11:13.480
I'll certainly try very hard, Howdy Doody.

11:13.480 --> 11:16.480
Maybe I can think of some kind of a trick,

11:16.480 --> 11:19.480
an old cowboy trick that I might have learned way back there.

11:19.480 --> 11:21.480
Oh, gee, thanks, Ray.

11:21.480 --> 11:23.480
A trick would be good if you can dig one up.

11:23.480 --> 11:26.480
So, Clarabel, you open up the scope doodle,

11:26.480 --> 11:29.480
and when the movie's over, maybe Ray will have something for it.

11:29.480 --> 11:32.480
That's a good idea, Clarabel.

11:32.480 --> 11:33.480
You open the...

11:33.480 --> 11:35.480
Oh, that's right, the sign.

11:35.480 --> 11:38.480
Mr. Buster's sign has to go on the scope doodle curtains.

11:38.480 --> 11:39.480
Oh, golly.

11:39.480 --> 11:42.480
Well, I'll try to think of a trick while the movie's going on.

11:42.480 --> 11:44.480
I'll go over here and watch it with the kids.

11:49.480 --> 11:51.480
Now, here we go with our old-time movie.

11:55.480 --> 11:57.480
There, Clarabel's got it all adjusted.

11:57.480 --> 11:59.480
It's gonna be in focus.

11:59.480 --> 12:01.480
Move over here a little closer.

12:01.480 --> 12:03.480
That's a boy.

12:04.480 --> 12:06.480
Can you all see all right now?

12:06.480 --> 12:07.480
Fine. See?

12:07.480 --> 12:10.480
Now, this is a very interesting picture.

12:10.480 --> 12:13.480
Harry Langdon, you've seen him before, I think.

12:13.480 --> 12:15.480
He's the young man who just got married,

12:15.480 --> 12:17.480
and that's his very pretty bride.

12:17.480 --> 12:19.480
But he has nothing but bad luck.

12:19.480 --> 12:21.480
Just coming out of the church, a horse shoe falls down

12:21.480 --> 12:23.480
and hits him right on the head.

12:23.480 --> 12:25.480
He says, Well, it's all right.

12:25.480 --> 12:28.480
Drops it in the box and hits a mirror,

12:28.480 --> 12:31.480
which is also supposed to be bad luck.

12:31.480 --> 12:35.480
Well, he feels a little unhappy about that,

12:35.480 --> 12:37.480
but he says, Oh, that's all right.

12:37.480 --> 12:39.480
We'll make out fine.

12:39.480 --> 12:41.480
There's platters.

12:41.480 --> 12:44.480
So anyhow, they get in the car,

12:44.480 --> 12:47.480
and they're going on their honeymoon.

12:47.480 --> 12:50.480
And what do they do but miss the boat?

12:50.480 --> 12:52.480
They were gonna take a cruise.

12:54.480 --> 12:56.480
So in the meantime,

12:56.480 --> 12:58.480
Harry is the captain of an old ship,

12:58.480 --> 13:00.480
and he is looking for help.

13:00.480 --> 13:02.480
So while...

13:02.480 --> 13:04.480
Uh-oh.

13:04.480 --> 13:07.480
That is one way of getting a crew.

13:07.480 --> 13:09.480
He knocked them out.

13:09.480 --> 13:12.480
And he's going to be shanghaied

13:12.480 --> 13:15.480
and taken aboard this ship with his bride.

13:15.480 --> 13:19.480
Well, here they are out on the middle of the ocean.

13:19.480 --> 13:21.480
And there's poor, poor Harry over there,

13:21.480 --> 13:23.480
dressed in a sailor suit, and he says,

13:23.480 --> 13:25.480
Now, look, I've got to get out of here.

13:25.480 --> 13:28.480
I just got married, and my poor wife is waiting for me.

13:28.480 --> 13:31.480
He doesn't realize that she's also on board.

13:31.480 --> 13:33.480
So he says, Let me out of here,

13:33.480 --> 13:35.480
and he opens a port hole,

13:35.480 --> 13:37.480
and of course all the water comes in.

13:39.480 --> 13:41.480
See, the boat's very heavy,

13:41.480 --> 13:44.480
and it's way, way down in the water.

13:46.480 --> 13:48.480
So finally he goes upstairs,

13:48.480 --> 13:51.480
or up on deck there,

13:51.480 --> 13:53.480
and he sees this line of people

13:53.480 --> 13:55.480
all waiting to talk to the captain,

13:55.480 --> 13:57.480
because all of the sailors are very unhappy

13:57.480 --> 13:59.480
about conditions on the ship.

13:59.480 --> 14:02.480
So he gets in the line with them.

14:03.480 --> 14:05.480
Well, while these sailors are waiting

